{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"strict"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For example, if searching for Feb 29 in the Gregorian calendar, the algorithm may choose March 1 instead (for example, if the year is not a leap year). If you wish to find the next Feb 29 without the algorithm adjusting the next higher component in the specified ","type":"text"},{"code":"DateComponents","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"strict","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" option.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"There are ultimately implementation-defined limits in how far distant the search will go.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"FoundationEssentials"}],"fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"strict","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"case","roleHeading":"Case","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:20FoundationEssentials8CalendarV14MatchingPolicyO6strictyA2EmF","platforms":[{"introducedAt":"8.0","beta":false,"name":"iOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"8.0","beta":false,"name":"iPadOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"8.0","beta":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"10.10","beta":false,"name":"macOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"9.0","beta":false,"name":"tvOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"2.0","beta":false,"name":"watchOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false}],"title":"Calendar.MatchingPolicy.strict"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/calen